 "description": "Charge-symmetric / charge-antisymmetric decomposition of the A=3 3-body cumulant b3 and of every candidate 3-body object in the corpus. 3H and 3He are mirror nuclei, so b3(3H)-b3(3He) is exactly the binding difference and is the Coulomb displacement up to the Nolen-Schiffer residual. FINDINGS: (1) the chirality route's '10-24x' magnitude gap is one number per variant on the symmetric part -- 14.5x (2-bond), 8.4x (triangle-closed) -- the range was Coulomb splitting leaking into a strong-channel comparison; (2) every chiral variant, including triangle-closed and long-range, has a WRONG-SIGNED charge asymmetry, so the inversion is not an artifact of the 2-adjacent-bond truncation; (3) no candidate supplies more than ~22% of the Coulomb displacement and the per-bond factors carry no EM term, so the A=3 charge asymmetry is a missing CHANNEL, not a wrong 3-body operator. Scope-limited: n=2 atoms, a decomposition rather than a closure. Exploratory; no production wiring, no fit.",
